<%#
  The USDC-on-Solana mark: the USDC disc with the Solana bars badged on its
  bottom-right corner, the way a chain badge sits on a token everywhere else in
  crypto. On the Get USDC card it is the ONLY statement of the chain: that
  card's copy names USDC and digital dollars and never says Solana, so the
  badge carries "and it lives on Solana" by itself. The aria-label below is
  the same fact for a screen reader.

  COMPOSED FROM THE SHIPPED ASSETS, NOT REDRAWN. public/usdc-mark.svg and
  public/solana-mark.svg are the real brand files. The USDC path lives only
  there; the Solana path is ALREADY hand-copied inline in
  contests/_hero.html.erb, so a copy here would be its THIRD. Either way it is a
  copy of a brand that is not ours to restyle, and copies drift. They are <img>
  so the originals stay the single source.

  The badge sits in a ring of the CARD's background rather than a fixed colour,
  so the notch it cuts out of the disc reads as a gap in both themes instead of a
  grey smudge in one of them.

  Locals:
    size  (Integer, default 64) — px edge of the USDC disc. The badge scales with
          it at the ratio the operator's reference uses (~0.42).
%>
<%
  size  = local_assigns.fetch(:size, 64)
  badge = (size * 0.42).round
  ring  = (badge * 0.13).round
%>
<span class="relative inline-block flex-shrink-0"
      style="width:<%= size %>px;height:<%= size %>px"
      data-usdc-solana-mark
      aria-label="USDC on Solana" role="img">
  <img src="/usdc-mark.svg" alt="" width="<%= size %>" height="<%= size %>"
       class="block w-full h-full" data-mark="usdc">
  <span class="absolute rounded-full flex items-center justify-center bg-surface"
        style="width:<%= badge + ring * 2 %>px;height:<%= badge + ring * 2 %>px;right:<%= -ring %>px;bottom:<%= -ring %>px">
    <img src="/solana-mark.svg" alt="" width="<%= badge %>" height="<%= badge %>"
         class="block rounded-full bg-black p-[15%]"
         style="width:<%= badge %>px;height:<%= badge %>px" data-mark="solana">
  </span>
</span>
